# Joo Dee, One of Many: "{B}, {T}: Surveil 1. Create a token that's a copy of this creature, then sacrifice an artifact or creature.
# Activate only as a sorcery." Bot1 controls only Joo Dee (the Black Lotus that cast it is gone): she is summoning-sick on turn 1
# but {T} is still refused then (CR 302.6), and in the turn-3 main phase the surveil puts the top Mountain into the graveyard, the
# copy is made, and the sacrifice must be one of the two (the ruling): Bot1 sacrifices the token, so the tapped original stays.
# The copy was made before the sacrifice, or the sacrifice could not have been the token.

